====Noun====
# [[detraction]], [[blasphemy]], to hold in derision, [[vilify]]

==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|huspaz|derision, mockery|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kūd-|to mock|lang=ang}}. Related to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hyspan||to mock, scorn, deride|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|husc|hūsc|mockery, derision, scorn, insult|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|hosc||shame, ridicule, scorn|lang=goh}}.

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m|pl=hospas|head=hosp}}

# [[reproach]], [[contempt]], [[contumely]], [[insult]], [[blasphemy]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|hosp|}}

====Related terms====
* [[hospcwide]] m. insulting speech
* [[hospettan]] to ridicule 
* [[hospspræc|hospsprǣċ]] f. jeer, taunt 
* [[hospul]] contemptible 
* [[hospword]] n. abusive language, contemptuous expression

